 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on g_agamma from Fig. 6 ('This work', blue curve) of the paper, extracted from the vector PDF magP-8h-axion-coupling-95CL-zoomin.pdf in the arXiv e-print. Axis calibration verified three ways: top (f_a [Hz]) and bottom (m_a [eV]) axes consistent via m_a=2*pi*hbar*f to <0.1% of a decade; extracted minimum g=3.5e-13 GeV^-1 at m_a=2.8e-14 eV matches the abstract's ~4e-13 at ~3e-14 eV; extracted value at f=0.263 Hz is 1.30e-11 GeV^-1 vs quoted 1.3e-11. The plotted curve spans m_a ~ 6e-17 to 1.9e-13 eV (0.015-45 Hz), wider than the 0.43-43.9 Hz range where the text quotes the limit; full plotted curve reported. Raw polyline (1663 vertices, spiky at candidate/noisy frequencies) downsampled to per-log-bin medians (100 bins). Assumes local DM density rho=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Sec. II). Limit does not apply at the 342 candidate frequencies (SNR>2), which appear as narrow gaps in the excluded region.",
